\ case / of / endof / endcase — pattern dispatch by unification. A clause
\ pattern is ordinary code; matching commits its bindings and drops selector
\ and pattern; a mismatch rolls the bindings back and keeps the selector.
\ The default region before endcase owns the unmatched selector.

\ === ground values behave as equality ===

: kind case 1 of "one" endof 2 of "two" endof drop "many" endcase ;
1 kind . 2 kind . 5 kind . cr                 \ one two many

: color case :red of "warm" endof "str" of "text" endof 1/2 of "half" endof drop "?" endcase ;
:red color . "str" color . 1/2 color . :blue color . cr  \ warm text half ?

clear
\ === frames match as open records ===

: msg case { :type :quit } of "bye" endof { :type :move } of "moved" endof drop "unknown" endcase ;
{ :type :quit :id 4 } msg . cr                \ bye (extra keys allowed)
{ :type :move :x 1 :y 2 } msg . cr            \ moved
{ :type :chat } msg . cr                      \ unknown

clear
\ === logic vars in a pattern bind for the body ===

: pick-second | ?x | case [ _ x ] of x ? endof drop null endcase ;
[ 1 2 ] pick-second . [ 7 9 ] pick-second . "nope" pick-second . cr  \ 2 9 null

: shape | ?x | case [ x x ] of "twins" endof [ x ] of "single" endof drop "other" endcase ;
[ 3 3 ] shape . [ 5 ] shape . [ 3 4 ] shape . cr  \ twins single other (a failed arm unbinds x)

clear
\ === the default region owns the selector ===

: describe case :ok of "fine" endof "unmatched: " . dup . drop "seen" endcase ;
:oops describe . cr                           \ unmatched:  :oops seen

clear
\ === nesting and quotations ===

: nested | ?x | case [ :a x ] of x ? case 1 of "a-one" endof drop "a-other" endcase endof drop "outer" endcase ;
[ :a 1 ] nested . [ :a 2 ] nested . [ :b 1 ] nested . cr  \ a-one a-other outer

[: case 5 of "five" endof drop "other" endcase :] to q
5 q execute . 6 q execute . cr                \ five other

clear
\ === unify? commits; matches? does not ===

lvar to W
[ 1 W ] [ 1 5 ] unify? . W ? . cr             \ 1 5
lvar to V
[ 2 V ] [ 1 5 ] unify? . V ? . cr             \ 0 ?V (rolled back on mismatch)

clear
\ === errors (each reason parenthesized) ===

1 2 of                                        \ (of outside case)
endcase                                       \ (endcase outside case)
: broken case 1 of "x" endof ;                \ (case with no endcase; definition rolls back)
broken                                        \ (the partial definition rolled back)
